Hm, I do indeed suspect that zero-variance cells would make the
car::Anova code (on which ezANOVA relies) choke. Is your data possibly
not in raw format? That is, is this number you have in prsp a summary
measure derived from some other more numerous measure? If this is the
case, you may be able to find a more appropriate model for the raw
data.

--
Mike Lawrence
Graduate Student
Department of Psychology & Neuroscience
Dalhousie University

~ Certainty is (possibly) folly ~

